course: dictionary
lesson: 587
title: Words about machines and work
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Automation means machines and computers doing work by themselves, without a person doing each step. A self-service till and an automatic door are small examples you may already have used.
explain: «Automation is machines doing work people did.» The sentence gives you the key idea: the work used to be done by people, and now a machine does it. Look for clues like "machines" and "people did" to work out the meaning.
explain: The word can also mean the system or machines that do this work, as in «factory automation». People disagree about whether automation helps or hurts jobs, so read carefully and ask what each side says.
fact: Automation is a noun. Its verb is automate, which means to make machines do a task.
fact: «Automation» means using machines and computers to do work by themselves.
fact: The word starts with «auto», which means self, as in automatic.
fact: Automation can replace some jobs but can also create new ones, and people disagree about whether it balances out.
fact: Common phrases are «home automation», «factory automation» and «due to automation».
exercise: «Automation is machines doing work people did.» What is the main idea? | Machines that never need to be switched on | People choosing to work in a team | *Machines doing work that people used to do | Jobs that are only done at night
exercise: A self-service till scans and bags your shopping without a cashier. What is this an example of? | Tidying | Gardening | *Automation
exercise: What is the verb form of automation? | Automobile | *Automate | Automatic
test: «One robot replacing 10 packers takes jobs, but new jobs appear too.» What does this sentence suggest about automation? | *Automation can replace some jobs and create others | Automation stops all work for ever | Automation can only make tea and coffee
test: Which phrase means automation used in a house? | Garden fencing | Factory automation | Hand washing | *Home automation
exam: Why do people disagree about automation? | Because it is always cheaper for everyone | Because it only happens in schools | *Because it can replace some jobs but also create new ones, and people disagree about whether it balances out | Because it never does any work at all
